 # Multi-Level Hashed Grid Construction
 
-Also called: Grid Encoding (Hash Grid), Hash Grid, Hashed grid with macrocells, Multi-Level Hashed Grid, Row Displacement Compressed Grid
+Also called: Grid Encoding (Hash Grid), Hash Grid, Hashed grid with macrocells, Multi-Level Hashed Grid, Multi-level Hash Tables, Row Displacement Compressed Grid
 
 ## Overview
-Multi-Level Hashed Grid Construction is a method for rapidly building a sparse acceleration structure for volume rendering and ray tracing that combines the memory efficiency of hashed grids with the traversal speed of multi-level structures [S1, S2, unofficial]. It solves the problem of high memory consumption in classic multi-level array grids and the poor traversal performance of one-level hashed grids by using row displacement compression to eliminate empty cells and macrocells to skip large empty regions [S1, unofficial]. Unlike its sibling [Hash Grids](936-hash-grids.md), which uses a single resolution level, this method employs multiple resolutions to balance detail and coverage, and unlike [Voxel World Data Structure](1101-voxel-world-data-structure.md), it avoids storing explicit empty voxels by compressing the grid topology [S1, unofficial].
+Multi-Level Hashed Grid Construction is a method for rapidly building a sparse acceleration structure for volume rendering that combines the memory efficiency of hashed grids with the traversal speed of multi-level structures [S1, S2, unofficial]. It solves the problem of high memory consumption in classic multi-level array grids and the poor render performance of one-level hashed grids on large, sparse scenes [S1, unofficial]. It sets itself apart from its parent [Hash Grids](936-hash-grids.md) by adding a hierarchical macrocell layer to skip empty regions in larger steps, and from [Voxel World Data Structure](1101-voxel-world-data-structure.md) by using row displacement compression to avoid storing empty cells entirely [S1, unofficial].
 
 ## How it works
-The method constructs a hierarchical grid structure in two main phases: building the compressed hash table for the finest level and constructing macrocells for coarser levels [S1, S2, unofficial].
+The method constructs a multi-resolution hash table for feature storage and a macrocell structure for spatial traversal. It uses row displacement compression to map 3D coordinates to a compact hash table, ensuring no memory is wasted on empty cells [S1, unofficial].
 
