 ### Multigrid Volume Compression Header Generation
-An algorithm to generate compression headers for a multigrid volume representation [S3, unofficial]. It determines the dominant label and constant subregion status for each node in the hierarchy by analyzing child elements [S3, unofficial]. It initializes a constant flag, iterates through 8 children (skipping those with label `0xFFFFFFFF`), counts label occurrences to find the max label, and updates the constant flag only if all children are constant and share the same label [S3, unofficial]. It writes the max label and constant flag to the output array and updates the LOD start index by adding `current_dim^3` [S3, unofficial].
+An algorithm to generate compression headers for a multigrid volume representation [S4, unofficial]. It determines the dominant label and constant subregion status for each node in the hierarchy by analyzing child elements [S4, unofficial]. It iterates through 8 child elements, skipping those with label `0xFFFFFFFF` (outside volume), counts label occurrences to find the max label, and updates a constant flag if all children share the same label and are constant [S4, unofficial]. It writes the max label and constant flag to the output array and updates the LOD start position [S4, unofficial].
 
 ## Operating characteristics
--   **Time Complexity:** Linear in the number of scene items $N_I$, except for hash function computation which has a worst-case complexity of $O(M \times 4/3)$, where $M$ is the number of cells in the grid [S1, unofficial].
--   **Memory Complexity:** Roughly one order of magnitude lower than regular, non-compressed multi-level array grids [S1, unofficial]. Multi-level hashed grids have slightly higher memory consumption than one-level hashed grids due to the macrocell structures [S1, unofficial].
--   **Performance:** Multi-level hashed grids provide around twice the render time performance of one-level hashed grids for large scanned scenes with many empty cells, due to macrocells [S1, unofficial]. Build times are short and roughly linear with the number of triangles [S1, unofficial].
--   **Strengths:** Low memory footprint, fast build time, good render performance for large sparse scenes.
--   **Limitations:** Less effective for small, non-uniform density scenes compared to adaptive array grids [S1, unofficial].
